With this in place:

  * Each pool (and lane) shape carries a boolean `isHorizontal` flag on the shape data  
  * The external label never falls “off” the side of a vertical pool: we swap its box so it lands in the right place  
  * Down the road you could even hook into the renderer and apply an SVG rotation if you want the text drawn vertically – but swapping the bounds already brings the label back into a visible, correctly‐sized rectangle along the side of your vertical pool.
